{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEN49gpFAGkwL5EGM13R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CaHWuwuQ259k2m8Fd3gwL6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-LZV24o && python3 - <<'E'\nimport re\ns=open('server.py').read()\ns=s.replace('DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\\n','')\ns=s.replace('''    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n    if not refresh:\n        log(f\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expires_in}s\")\n''','''    # Intervals tokens are long-lived: no refresh_token, no expires_in. They die only on revocation (seen as a 401).\n    expires_in = int(tok[\"expires_in\"]) if tok.get(\"expires_in\") else None\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n''')\ns=s.replace('\"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in,','\"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in if expires_in else None,')\ns=s.replace('(expires in {expires_in}s)\")','(expires_in={expires_in})\")')\ns=s.replace('''if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:''','''if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] is None or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:''')\ns=s.replace('''        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            self.send_json(e.code, {\"error\": f\"intervals returned {e.code}\"})''','''        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            if e.code == 401:  # revoked on the Intervals side\n                with LOCK:\n                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n            self.send_json(e.code, {\"error\": f\"intervals returned {e.code}\"})''')\ns=s.replace('''        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n            return self.auth_init()\n''','')\ns=s.replace('''        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/disconnect\":''','''        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n            return self.auth_init()\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/disconnect\":''')\ns=s.replace('''        self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\"))''','''        self.send_json(200, {\"authorize_url\": AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\")})''')\nopen('server.py','w').write(s)\nc=open('config.py').read()\nc=c.replace('ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE','ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE')\nopen('config.py','w').write(c)\na=open('static/app.js').read()\na=a.replace('<a class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">Connect Intervals.icu</a>','<button class=\"btn\" id=\"connect\">Connect Intervals.icu</button>')\na=a.replace('''    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");''','''    const cn = document.getElementById(\"connect\");\n    if (cn) cn.onclick = async () => {\n      try { window.location.assign((await api(\"/api/intervals/auth/init\", { method: \"POST\" })).authorize_url); }\n      catch (e) { root.innerHTML = `<p class=\"card\">Error: ${esc(e.message)}</p>`; }\n    };\n    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");''')\nopen('static/app.js','w').write(a)\nE\npython3 -m py_compile server.py && rm -rf __pycache__\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Intervals.icu connect failures — causes and fixes\n\n1. **Connect button always 401 (all athletes).** The button was a plain link to `GET /api/intervals/auth/init`. A full-page navigation does not send the `Authorization` header the SPA keeps in localStorage, so `require_user` returned 401 (ticket #214, log section 1). Fix: init is now an authenticated `POST` returning `{authorize_url}` as JSON (`server.py`); the SPA calls it via the fetch wrapper and does `window.location.assign(authorize_url)` (`static/app.js`). The callback stays an unauthenticated GET; identity travels in the signed `state`.\n2. **Authorize URL rejected with 400 `invalid_request` since 2026-10-02.** `config.SCOPES` named `ACTIVITY` and `CALENDAR` twice (`:READ` and `:WRITE`). `:WRITE` implies `:READ`, and Intervals rejects repeats (the colleague's \"Duplicate scope\"; our 400 body doesn't name it, but this is the only malformed parameter and matches the timing of the calendar-sync change). Now `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`. Not verified against the live Intervals service.\n3. **Connection \"expired\" after an hour.** Intervals tokens have no `refresh_token` and no `expires_in`; they last until revoked. Our code invented a 3600s default TTL and the refresher marked tokens expired with no refresh token (log: Rivera, 2026-09-19). Fix: removed the default TTL; `expires_at` is `None` when the provider gives none and the refresher skips such tokens. Revocation is handled lazily: a 401 from the Intervals API marks the connection \"expired, reconnect\" and clears the token.\n\n## Colleague's note: what applied\n- Applied: no refresh_token / never expires (#3), duplicate scope (#2), GET→POST init (#1), lazy 401 handling.\n- Not applied: `SETTINGS:WRITE` scope (we don't need it); the token exchange without `grant_type`/`redirect_uri` (our exchange demonstrably worked in the Rivera log, so left unchanged); JWT state, encryption at rest, and the account-mismatch guard (good hardening, but not causes here and out of scope; our HMAC state with a 15-minute TTL already works; tokens are still stored in plaintext in memory).\n\nNot tested end-to-end: no real Intervals credentials here; only a syntax check was run.\nE\ngit status --short"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5192,"cache_read_input_tokens":24287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5192},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_