{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEN5GrhCbEXioL3pPCAQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed all three causes in the code and wrote them up in `ANSWER.md`, which also says which parts of your colleague's note applied. I haven't tested the flow end to end. I have no real Intervals.icu credentials here, so I only syntax-checked `server.py`.\n\n1. **Connect button failing for everyone.** The button was a plain link to `GET /api/intervals/auth/init`. A full-page navigation doesn't send the `Authorization` header, so every request got a 401. Init is now an authenticated `POST` that returns `{authorize_url}` as JSON, and the page redirects the browser to that URL.\n2. **Authorize step rejected since the calendar sync shipped.** The scope list named `ACTIVITY` and `CALENDAR` twice, once as `:READ` and once as `:WRITE`. Intervals rejects repeats, and `:WRITE` already includes `:READ`. The scopes are now `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`. Intervals' 400 body doesn't name the offending parameter, so this is inferred from the timing and the colleague's note. I haven't confirmed it against Intervals.\n3. **Rivera told to reconnect after an hour.** Intervals tokens have no refresh token and no expiry. Our code assumed a 3600-second lifetime and marked the connection expired once that passed. I removed that default, and tokens without an expiry are no longer expired by the background refresher. If the Intervals API returns 401, the connection is now marked \"expired, reconnect\" and the token is cleared.\n\nFrom the colleague's note, I used the three points above (token lifetime, duplicate scope, `POST` init). I did not add the `SETTINGS:WRITE` scope, since we don't need it. I also left the token exchange alone, because it worked in Rivera's log. The JWT state, encryption at rest and account-mismatch guard are good hardening but weren't causes here, so I left them out. Tokens are still stored unencrypted in memory.\n\nThe changes are in `server.py`, `config.py` and `static/app.js`, and nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2475,"cache_read_input_tokens":29479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2475},"output_tokens":705,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad1d2442-c4da-4707-83fc-ea5dc62e2a07","uuid":"5be39496-53a4-4b6f-8de0-eb58c5888046","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:34:03.051Z","request_id":"req_011CgEN5GV7ZuSGXnQCEGQxQ"}
